    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67000" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετατύ̆π-ωσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>transformation</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ammon.
				<u>Diff.</u>
				p.91
			</span></i> V. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>conversion</i> of a compound word into two simple ones, as
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρόπολις</span> into <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκρα πόλις</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				626.49
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				75.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> defined as
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέξις ἐνηλλαγμένα στοιχεῖα
			ἔχουσα</span> (as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπαί</span> for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπό</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Trypho
				<u>Trop.</u>
				2.16
			</span></i>.</div>
